comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T15:37:37.458Z",claude,"The per-field merge is proven against two real branches rather than a simulated merge: two reviewers writing different fields of one review record both survive, a reviewers-set addition from each side survives, and a genuinely conflicting scalar is still reported as a conflict while the other fields merge. approved_at is treated as a timestamp that converges to the latest, and createReviewRecord omits absent optional fields so an unset field does not merge as a deletion."
  "2026-08-28T20:11:18.321Z",pi-agent,"PR #48 evidence: real-branch review merges passed inside the 675-test suite, including disjoint fields, reviewer-set union, timestamp convergence, and isolated scalar conflict. npm run release:check passed with c8 at 100 percent statements branches and lines. This child remains closed."
